Chr4	Araport11	gene	1101378	1103612	.	+	.	ID=AT4G02500;Name=AT4G02500;Note=UDP-xylosyltransferase 2;curator_summary=Encodes a protein with xylosyltransferase activity%2C which is specific for UDP-xylose as donor substrate and for oligosaccharides with a degree of polymerization %3E4. Although the enzyme utilizes either cellopentaose or cellohexaose%2C its activity is four-fold higher with cellohexaose as an acceptor compared to cellopentaose. The enzyme is able to add several xylosyl residues to the acceptor forming mono-%2C di- and trixylosylated polysaccharides.;symbol=XT2;Alias=ATXT2,ARABIDOPSIS THALIANA UDP-XYLOSYLTRANSFERASE 2,AtXXT2,XXT2,XYG XYLOSYLTRANSFERASE 2;full_name=UDP-xylosyltransferase 2;computational_description=UDP-xylosyltransferase 2 (XT2)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: xyloglucan 6-xylosyltransferase activity%2C UDP-xylosyltransferase activity%2C transferase activity%2C transferring glycosyl groups%2C transferase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: polysaccharide biosynthetic process%2C xyloglucan biosynthetic process%2C root hair elongation%3B LOCATED IN: mitochondrion%2C integral to membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 22 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Galactosyl transferase (InterPro:IPR008630)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: xylosyltransferase 1 (TAIR:AT3G62720.2)%3B Has 461 Blast hits to 460 proteins in 94 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 6%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 152%3B Plants - 284%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 19 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12011320,PMID:12032363,PMID:15295017,PMID:16798886,PMID:16982611,PMID:17286857,PMID:18544630,PMID:18557833,PMID:18650403,PMID:18805951,PMID:22108526,PMID:22362871,PMID:22665445,PMID:22696020,PMID:22670626,PMID:24834920,PMID:25392066,PMID:25604050,locus:2132293;locus_type=protein_coding
