Chr4	Araport11	gene	1143888	1147562	.	+	.	ID=AT4G02600;Name=AT4G02600;Note=Seven transmembrane MLO family protein;curator_summary=A member of a large family of seven-transmembrane domain proteins specific to plants%2C homologs of the barley mildew resistance locus o (MLO) protein. The Arabidopsis genome contains 15 genes encoding MLO proteins%2C with localization in plasma membrane. Phylogenetic analysis revealed four clades of closely-related AtMLO genes. ATMLO1 belongs to the clade II%2C with ATMLO13 and ATMLO15. The gene is expressed during early seedling growth%2C in root and cotyledon vascular system%2C in pollen and in papillae%2C as shown by GUS activity patterns. The expression of several phylogenetically closely-related AtMLO genes showed similar or overlapping tissue specificity and analogous responsiveness to external stimuli%2C suggesting functional redundancy%2C co-function%2C or antagonistic function(s).;symbol=MLO1;computational_description=MLO1%3B FUNCTIONS IN: calmodulin binding%3B INVOLVED IN: cell death%2C defense response%3B LOCATED IN: plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 27 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 15 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Mlo-related protein (InterPro:IPR004326)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Seven transmembrane MLO family protein (TAIR:AT2G44110.1)%3B Has 552 Blast hits to 532 proteins in 57 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 548%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 4 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12569425,PMID:15060130,PMID:16359384,PMID:16525893,PMID:18184068,PMID:25187041,PMID:25506769,locus:2132313;locus_type=protein_coding
