Chr4	Araport11	gene	2664314	2666973	.	+	.	ID=AT4G05160;Name=AT4G05160;Note=AMP-dependent synthetase and ligase family protein;curator_summary=Encodes a peroxisomal protein involved in the activation of fatty acids through esterification with CoA. At4g05160 preferentially activates fatty acids with medium chain length (C6:0 and C7:0) as well as even-numbered long-chain fatty acids (C14:0%2C  C16:0 and C18:0). At4g05160 was also able to catalyze the conversion of OPC-6:0 to its CoA ester and is therefore thought to be involved in the peroxisomal %26#946%3B-oxidation steps of jasmonic acid biosynthesis.;computational_description=AMP-dependent synthetase and ligase family protein%3B FUNCTIONS IN: 4-coumarate-CoA ligase activity%2C fatty-acyl-CoA synthase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: jasmonic acid biosynthetic process%3B LOCATED IN: peroxisome%3B EXPRESSED IN: 22 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: AMP-binding%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR020845)%2C AMP-dependent synthetase/ligase (InterPro:IPR000873)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: OPC-8:0 CoA ligase1 (TAIR:AT1G20510.1)%3B Has 86858 Blast hits to 79133 proteins in 3797 species: Archae - 1159%3B Bacteria - 54259%3B Metazoa - 3570%3B Fungi - 4802%3B Plants - 2877%3B Viruses - 1%3B Other Eukaryotes - 20190 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12805634,PMID:14568076,PMID:14612585,PMID:14701923,PMID:15377757,PMID:15878986,PMID:16099486,PMID:16256065,PMID:16776291,PMID:16963437,PMID:17254327,PMID:17951448,PMID:18650403,PMID:18805951,PMID:18931141,locus:2115673;locus_type=protein_coding
