Chr4	Araport11	mRNA	7201656	7208937	.	+	.	ID=AT4G12020.1;Parent=AT4G12020;Name=AT4G12020.1;Note=protein kinase family protein;curator_summary=Encodes a member of the A1 subgroup of the MEKK (MAPK/ERK kinase kinase) family. MEKK is another name for Mitogen-Activated Protein Kinase Kinase Kinase (MAPKKK or MAP3K).  This subgroup has four members: At4g08500 (MEKK1%2C also known as ARAKIN%2C MAP3Kb1%2C MAPKKK8)%2C At4g08480 (MEKK2%2C also known as MAP3Kb4%2C MAPKKK9)%2C  At4g08470 (MEKK3%2C also known as MAP3Kb3%2C MAPKKK10) and At4g12020 (MEKK4%2C also known as MAP3Kb5%2C MAPKKK11%2C WRKY19).  Nomenclatures for mitogen-activated protein kinases are described in Trends in Plant Science 2002%2C7(7):301.;conf_class=6;symbol=WRKY19;computational_description=WRKY19%3B FUNCTIONS IN: protein binding%2C sequence-specific DNA binding transcription factor activity%3B INVOLVED IN: in 7 processes%3B LOCATED IN: chloroplast envelope%3B EXPRESSED IN: 22 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 14 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: NB-ARC (InterPro:IPR002182)%2C Leucine-rich repeat (InterPro:IPR001611)%2C Disease resistance protein (InterPro:IPR000767)%2C Toll-Interleukin receptor (InterPro:IPR000157)%2C Serine/threonine-protein kinase-like domain (InterPro:IPR017442)%2C Protein kinase-like domain (InterPro:IPR011009)%2C DNA-binding WRKY (InterPro:IPR003657)%2C ATPase%2C AAA+ type%2C core (InterPro:IPR003593)%2C Protein kinase%2C catalytic domain (InterPro:IPR000719)%2C EGF-like (InterPro:IPR006210)%2C Paired amphipathic helix (InterPro:IPR003822)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: nucleoside-triphosphatases%3Btransmembrane receptors%3Bnucleotide binding%3BATP binding (TAIR:AT4G19500.1)%3B Has 144103 Blast hits to 127280 proteins in 3862 species: Archae - 77%3B Bacteria - 12337%3B Metazoa - 45865%3B Fungi - 10852%3B Plants - 56227%3B Viruses - 349%3B Other Eukaryotes - 18396 (source: NCBI BLink).;conf_rating=**;Dbxref=PMID:11118137,PMID:12938931,gene:2118115,UniProt:B3H4T8
