Chr4	Araport11	gene	7585869	7587099	.	-	.	ID=AT4G12970;Name=AT4G12970;Note=stomagen;curator_summary=Encodes a cysteine-rich peptide%2C a secretory factor that is produced in the mesophyll cells and acts on the epidermis to increase stomatal formation.  Its mature form is a 45-aa peptide with three intramolecular disulfide bonds.  It is proposed that STOMAGEN increases stomatal number by competing with two negative regulators of stomatal density%2C EPF1 and EPF2%2C possibly through direct interaction with the receptor-like protein TMM. Its transcript levels change after inducing MUTE expression in a mute background.;symbol=STOMAGEN;Alias=AtEPFL9,EPFL9;full_name=STOMAGEN;computational_description=STOMAGEN (STOMAGEN)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: molecular_function unknown%3B INVOLVED IN: stomatal complex patterning%2C regulation of stomatal complex development%2C positive regulation of stomatal complex development%2C cell-cell signaling%3B LOCATED IN: endomembrane system%3B EXPRESSED IN: 19 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 12 growth stages%3B Has 29 Blast hits to 29 proteins in 10 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 29%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 0 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12805589,PMID:18650403,PMID:20010603,PMID:20007289,PMID:20149115,PMID:21509541,PMID:22027592,PMID:22232766,PMID:22819466,PMID:23432385,PMID:23686240,PMID:23662679,PMID:23748792,PMID:23997204,PMID:25267734,PMID:23755192,locus:2123261;locus_type=protein_coding
