Chr4	Araport11	mRNA	7769770	7773666	.	-	.	ID=AT4G13350.1;Parent=AT4G13350;Name=AT4G13350.1;Note=NSP (nuclear shuttle protein)-interacting GTPase;curator_summary=Encodes a GTPase that interacts with nuclear shuttle proteins (NSPs) from a number of different plant viruses. The gene is widely expressed and NIG transcript levels do not rise in response to viral infection. This cytoplasmic protein does not directly interact with a viral movement protein (MP)%2C but%2C it does promote the movement of NSP from the nucleus to the cytoplasm. Overexpression of NIG in Arabidopsis plants renders them more sensitive to geminivirus infection.;conf_class=2;symbol=NIG;full_name=NSP (nuclear shuttle protein)-interacting GTPase;computational_description=NSP (nuclear shuttle protein)-interacting GTPase (NIG)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: GTP binding%2C GTPase activity%3B INVOLVED IN: nucleocytoplasmic transport%2C response to virus%3B LOCATED IN: cytosol%2C cytoplasm%3B EXPRESSED IN: flower%2C root%2C cultured cell%2C leaf%3B EXPRESSED DURING: seedling growth%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Arf GTPase activating protein (InterPro:IPR001164)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: ArfGap/RecO-like zinc finger domain-containing protein (TAIR:AT4G32630.1)%3B Has 7463 Blast hits to 6530 proteins in 396 species: Archae - 2%3B Bacteria - 285%3B Metazoa - 3343%3B Fungi - 1586%3B Plants - 848%3B Viruses - 60%3B Other Eukaryotes - 1339 (source: NCBI BLink).;conf_rating=****;Dbxref=PMID:18433157,gene:2142114,UniProt:Q8W4K6
