Chr4	Araport11	gene	8426677	8429720	.	-	.	ID=AT4G14713;Name=AT4G14713;Note=TIFY domain/Divergent CCT motif family protein;curator_summary=PPD1 (and its paralog%2C PPD2) encode plant-specific putative DNA-binding proteins. PPD1 and PPD2 are not found in grasses. Overexpression of PPD reduces lamina size by promoting the early arrest of dispersed meristematic cells DMC proliferation during leaf and silique development. Deletion of the PPD locus increases leaf lamina size and results in dome-shaped rather than flat leaves. Siliques are also altered in shape because of extra lamina growth. The curvature of a deltappd leaf reflects the difference between excess growth of the lamina and a limitation to the extension capacity of its perimeter.;symbol=PPD1;Alias=TIFY4A;full_name=PEAPOD 1;computational_description=PEAPOD 1 (PPD1)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Tify (InterPro:IPR010399)%2C Acireductone dioxygenase%2C ARD (InterPro:IPR004313)%2C CCT domain-like (InterPro:IPR018467)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: TIFY domain/Divergent CCT motif family protein (TAIR:AT4G14720.1)%3B Has 256 Blast hits to 255 proteins in 23 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 0%3B Metazoa - 0%3B Fungi - 0%3B Plants - 256%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 0 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:16916932,PMID:17499004,PMID:17675405,PMID:20032078,PMID:20360743,PMID:20460583,locus:505006464;locus_type=protein_coding
