Chr4	Araport11	gene	9269094	9271669	.	-	.	ID=AT4G16440;Name=AT4G16440;Note=ferredoxin hydrogenase;curator_summary=Encodes a [FeFe]-hydrogenase-like protein named Gollum (for Growth in different Oxygen LeveLs in%26#64258%3BUences Morphogenesis).  Heterologous expression of Gollum in E. coli indicates that it probably contains two [Fe-S] clusters with different magnetic properties. Sequence alignment analysis indicates that these two clusters would be topologically equivalent to the mesial and proximal [Fe-S] centers of [FeFe]-hydrogenases. Knockdown mutants (RNAi) show a dwarf phenotype at the normal atmospheric partial oxygen pressure of 21 kPa.  This dwarf phenotype could be rescued by growing the plant under low oxygen pressure (5kPa)%2C suggesting a role for this gene in oxygen sensing.;symbol=NAR1;Alias=GOLLUM,Growth at different Oxygen Levels Influences Morphogenesis;full_name=homolog of yeast NAR1;computational_description=ferredoxin hydrogenases%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Iron hydrogenase%2C large subunit%2C C-terminal (InterPro:IPR004108)%2C Iron hydrogenase (InterPro:IPR009016)%2C Iron hydrogenase%2C small subunit-like (InterPro:IPR003149)%3B Has 2574 Blast hits to 2544 proteins in 612 species: Archae - 1%3B Bacteria - 1826%3B Metazoa - 221%3B Fungi - 188%3B Plants - 72%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 266 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:18329103,PMID:18493040,PMID:18650403,PMID:20226671,PMID:22589469,PMID:23104832,PMID:23639116,PMID:23734982,locus:2130634;locus_type=protein_coding
