Chr4	Araport11	pseudogene	10038131	10041950	.	+	.	ID=AT4G18120;Name=AT4G18120;Note=MEI2-like 3;curator_summary=A member of mei2-like gene family%2C predominantly plant-based family of genes encoding RNA binding proteins with characteristic presence of a highly conserved RNA binding motif first described in the mei2 gene of the fission yeast S. pombe. In silico analyses reveal nine mei2 -like genes in A. thaliana. They were grouped into four distinct clades%2C based on overall sequence similarity and subfamily-specific sequence elements. AML3 is a member of two sister clades of mei2-like gene family%2C AML1 through AML5%2C and belongs to the clade named ALM235. Among mei2-like genes%2C AML3 is the transcript with highest frequency of alternative splicing. Expression was detected during early embryo development (heart and torpedo stage)%3B no accumulation was detected in vegetative and floral apices%2C as revealed by in situ hybridization.;symbol=ML3;Alias=AML3,MEI2-like 3;full_name=MEI2-like 3;computational_description=MEI2-like 3 (ML3)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: RNA binding%2C nucleotide binding%2C nucleic acid binding%3B INVOLVED IN: biological_process unknown%3B LOCATED IN: nucleus%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: RNA recognition motif%2C RNP-1 (InterPro:IPR000504)%2C RNA recognition motif 2 (InterPro:IPR007201)%2C Nucleotide-binding%2C alpha-beta plait (InterPro:IPR012677)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: MEI2-like protein 5 (TAIR:AT1G29400.2)%3B Has 2869 Blast hits to 2722 proteins in 297 species: Archae - 8%3B Bacteria - 173%3B Metazoa - 1272%3B Fungi - 326%3B Plants - 696%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 394 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:15356386,PMID:16473967,locus:2117706,PMID:15356386,PMID:16473967,locus:2117706;locus_type=pseudogene
