Chr4	Araport11	gene	10192909	10195662	.	+	.	ID=AT4G18470;Name=AT4G18470;Note=negative regulator of systemic acquired resistance (SNI1);curator_summary=Negative regulator of systemic acquired resistance (SAR)%2C repressor of pathogenesis-related PR gene expression which is removed by NPR1 upon induction of SAR. Encodes leucine-rich nuclear protein. Conserved in plants%2C with putative orthologs found in several plant species. Many NPR1-dependent PR gene are specifically derepressed in the sni1 mutant. The structural similarity of SNI1 to Armadillo repeat proteins implies that SNI1 may form a scaffold for interaction with proteins that modulate transcription. Histone modification may be involved in SNI1-mediated repression of PR genes.;symbol=SNI1;full_name=SUPPRESSOR OF NPR1-1%2C INDUCIBLE 1;computational_description=SUPPRESSOR OF NPR1-1%2C INDUCIBLE 1 (SNI1)%3B Has 30201 Blast hits to 17322 proteins in 780 species: Archae - 12%3B Bacteria - 1396%3B Metazoa - 17338%3B Fungi - 3422%3B Plants - 5037%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 2996 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:10458608,PMID:10339621,PMID:11387978,PMID:16809812,PMID:16766691,PMID:17360504,PMID:17369431,PMID:18321188,PMID:20935179,PMID:21149701,PMID:21139438,PMID:21320694,PMID:22589469,PMID:24207055,locus:2124534;locus_type=protein_coding
