Chr4	Araport11	mRNA	10940746	10943502	.	+	.	ID=AT4G20260.4;Parent=AT4G20260;Name=AT4G20260.4;Note=plasma-membrane associated cation-binding protein 1;curator_summary=Encodes a Ca2+ and Cu2+ binding protein. N-terminal myristylation on glycine 2 appears to enable it to associate tightly with the plasma membrane. Recombinant PCaP1 interacts strongly with phosphatidylinositol 3%2C5-bisphosphate (PtdIns(3%2C5)P2) and  PtdIns (3%2C4%2C5)P3%2C and weakly with PtdIns(3%2C5)P2 and PtdIns(4%2C5). It also interacts with calmodulin (CaM) in a calcium-dependent manner. CaM does not interfere with PCaP1 membrane localization but does weaken interactions between it and the PtdInsPs. PCaP1 has an apparent Kd of 10 uM for Cu2+ and can bind six ions per protein. Transcript levels for PCaP1 first fall and then rise following exposure to CuCl2. Mannitol%2C sorbitol%2C and the flg22 oligopeptide also increase expression levels.;conf_class=2;symbol=PCAP1;Alias=ATPCAP1,ARABIDOPSIS THALIANA PLASMA-MEMBRANE ASSOCIATED CATION-BINDING PROTEIN 1,MDP25,microtubule-destabilizing protein 25;full_name=plasma-membrane associated cation-binding protein 1;computational_description=plasma-membrane associated cation-binding protein 1 (PCAP1)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: calmodulin binding%2C copper ion binding%2C phosphatidylinositol-3%2C4%2C5-trisphosphate binding%2C phosphatidylinositol-3%2C5-bisphosphate binding%2C calcium ion binding%3B INVOLVED IN: response to cold%2C N-terminal peptidyl-glycine N-myristoylation%2C defense response to bacterium%3B LOCATED IN: plasma membrane%2C vacuole%3B EXPRESSED IN: 35 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 16 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: DREPP plasma membrane polypeptide (InterPro:IPR008469)%3B Has 35333 Blast hits to 34131 proteins in 2444 species: Archae - 798%3B Bacteria - 22429%3B Metazoa - 974%3B Fungi - 991%3B Plants - 531%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 9610 (source: NCBI BLink).;conf_rating=****;Dbxref=PMID:15539469,PMID:15971193,PMID:17028151