Chr4	Araport11	gene	11746490	11750698	.	-	.	ID=AT4G22200;Name=AT4G22200;Note=potassium transport 2/3;curator_summary=Encodes AKT2%2C a photosynthate- and light-dependent inward rectifying potassium channel with unique gating properties that are regulated by phosphorylation.  Expressed in guard cell protoplasts and in the phloem and xylem of aerial portions of the plant.  The channel can coassemble with another K+ channel%2C KAT1%2C in vitro.  In guard cells%2C AKT2/3 is responsible for the Ca2+ sensitivity of the K+ uptake channel.  In the phloem%2C it regulates the sucrose/H+ symporters via the phloem potential.  AKT2 belongs to the Shaker family K+ channels which include the following groups based on phylogenetic analysis (FEBS Letters (2007) 581: 2357): I (inward rectifying channel): AKT1 (AT2G26650)%2C AKT5 (AT4G32500) and SPIK (also known as AKT6%2C AT2G25600)%3B II (inward rectifying channel): KAT1 (AT5G46240) and KAT2 (AT4G18290)%3B III (weakly inward rectifying channel): AKT2 (AT4G22200)%3B IV (regulatory subunit involved in inwardly rectifying conductance formation): KAT3 (also known as AtKC1%2C AT4G32650)%3B V (outward rectifying channel): SKOR (AT3G02850) and GORK (AT5G37500).;symbol=KT2/3;Alias=AKT2,AKT2/3,potassium transport 2/3,AKT3;full_name=potassium transport 2/3;computational_description=potassium transport 2/3 (KT2/3)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: inward rectifier potassium channel activity%2C protein binding%2C cyclic nucleotide binding%3B INVOLVED IN: regulation of membrane potential%2C response to abscisic acid stimulus%3B LOCATED IN: membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 24 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 13 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Cyclic nucleotide-binding (InterPro:IPR000595)%2C Potassium channel%2C voltage-dependent%2C EAG/ELK/ERG (InterPro:IPR003938)%2C Protein of unknown function DUF3354 (InterPro:IPR021789)%2C Ankyrin repeat-containing domain (InterPro:IPR020683)%2C Ion transport (InterPro:IPR005821)%2C Cyclic nucleotide-binding-like (InterPro:IPR018490)%2C RmlC-like jelly roll fold (InterPro:IPR014710)%2C Ankyrin repeat (InterPro:IPR002110)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: K+ transporter 1 (TAIR:AT2G26650.1)%3B Has 30201 Blast hits to 17322 proteins in 780 species: Archae - 12%3B Bacteria - 1396%3B Metazoa - 17338%3B Fungi - 3422%3B Plants - 5037%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 2996 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:10929122,PMID:10852932,PMID:10377458,PMID:9916143,PMID:9707551,PMID:8549795,PMID:8552711,PMID:11706182,PMID:11226341,PMID:11181729,PMID:12172027,PMID:12034902,PMID:12447548,PMID:12678562,PMID:12795698,PMID:14675456,PMID:15299147,PMID:15824192,PMID:16316977,PMID:16297070,PMID:16968880,PMID:17146665,PMID:18650403,PMID:19748453,PMID:21187374,PMID:21445098,PMID:21445013,PMID:21518051,locus:2132065;locus_type=protein_coding
