Chr4	Araport11	gene	12574719	12577583	.	-	.	ID=AT4G24250;Name=AT4G24250;Note=Seven transmembrane MLO family protein;curator_summary=A member of a large family of seven-transmembrane domain proteins specific to plants%2C homologs of the barley mildew resistance locus o (MLO) protein. The Arabidopsis genome contains 15 genes encoding MLO proteins%2C with localization in plasma membrane. Phylogenetic analysis revealed four clades of closely-related AtMLO genes. ATMLO13 belongs to the clade II%2C with ATMLO1 and ATMLO15. The gene is expressed during early seedling growth%2C in root and cotyledon vascular system%2C in pollen and also in placenta of developing siliques%2C as shown by GUS activity patterns. The expression of several phylogenetically closely-related AtMLO genes showed similar or overlapping tissue specificity and analogous responsiveness to external stimuli%2C suggesting functional redundancy%2C co-function%2C or antagonistic function(s).;symbol=MLO13;Alias=ATMLO13,MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 13;full_name=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 13;computational_description=MILDEW RESISTANCE LOCUS O 13 (MLO13)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: calmodulin binding%3B INVOLVED IN: cell death%2C defense response%3B LOCATED IN: integral to membrane%2C plasma membrane%3B EXPRESSED IN: 13 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: seedling growth%2C petal differentiation and expansion stage%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Mlo-related protein (InterPro:IPR004326)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: Seven transmembrane MLO family protein (TAIR:AT4G02600.2)%3B Has 30201 Blast hits to 17322 proteins in 780 species: Archae - 12%3B Bacteria - 1396%3B Metazoa - 17338%3B Fungi - 3422%3B Plants - 5037%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 2996 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12569425,PMID:16146321,PMID:16525893,PMID:17064408,PMID:25506769,locus:2135982;locus_type=protein_coding
