Chr4	Araport11	gene	14447338	14448698	.	+	.	ID=AT4G29340;Name=AT4G29340;Note=profilin 4;curator_summary=Profilin is a low-molecular weight%2C actin monomer-binding protein that regulates the organization of actin cytoskeleton in eukaryotes%2C including higher plants. PRF4 and PRF5 are late pollen-specific and are not detectable in other cell types of the plant body including microspores and root hairs. Immunocytochemical studies at the subcellular level reveal that both the constitutive and pollen-specific profilins are abundant in the cytoplasm. In vegetative cell types%2C such as root apical cells%2C profilins showed localization to nuclei in addition to the cytoplasmic staining.;symbol=PRF4;full_name=profilin 4;computational_description=profilin 4 (PRF4)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: actin binding%3B INVOLVED IN: cytoskeleton organization%2C actin cytoskeleton organization%3B LOCATED IN: nucleus%2C actin cytoskeleton%2C cytoplasm%3B EXPRESSED IN: 11 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: L mature pollen stage%2C M germinated pollen stage%2C 4 anthesis%2C petal differentiation and expansion stage%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Profilin/allergen (InterPro:IPR002097)%2C Profilin%2C plant (InterPro:IPR005455)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: profilin 5 (TAIR:AT2G19770.1)%3B Has 899 Blast hits to 898 proteins in 239 species: Archae - 0%3B Bacteria - 2%3B Metazoa - 128%3B Fungi - 117%3B Plants - 583%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 69 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:8685262,PMID:12805594,PMID:14500793,PMID:15489280,PMID:15469496,PMID:16247729,PMID:16242667,PMID:16313636,PMID:16299181,PMID:17538023,PMID:18319396,PMID:18775970,PMID:21798377,locus:2118309;locus_type=protein_coding
