Chr4	Araport11	gene	17187528	17192507	.	-	.	ID=AT4G36380;Name=AT4G36380;Note=Cytochrome P450 superfamily protein;curator_summary=Encodes a cytochrome P-450 gene that is involved in leaf blade expansion by controlling polar cell expansion in the leaf length direction. Member of the CYP90C CYP450 family. ROT3 was shown to be involved in brassinosteroid biosynthesis%2C most likely in the conversion step of typhasterol (TY) to castasterone (CS). As 6-deoxo-CS was unable to restore the phenotype of rot3-1%2C it has been postulated that ROT3 might be specifically involved in the conversion of TY to CS in the C6-oxidation pathway of brassinolide. Recently%2C CYP90C1 was shown to catalyse the C-23 hydroxylation of several brassinosteroids (the enzyme has a broad specificity for 22-hydroxylated substrates).;symbol=ROT3;full_name=ROTUNDIFOLIA 3;computational_description=ROTUNDIFOLIA 3 (ROT3)%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Cytochrome P450 (InterPro:IPR001128)%2C Cytochrome P450%2C E-class%2C group IV (InterPro:IPR002403)%2C Cytochrome P450%2C conserved site (InterPro:IPR017972)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: cytochrome P450%2C family 90%2C subfamily D%2C polypeptide 1 (TAIR:AT3G13730.1)%3B Has 30201 Blast hits to 17322 proteins in 780 species: Archae - 12%3B Bacteria - 1396%3B Metazoa - 17338%3B Fungi - 3422%3B Plants - 5037%3B Viruses - 0%3B Other Eukaryotes - 2996 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:10430960,PMID:9694802,PMID:8625845,PMID:11978864,PMID:12226529,PMID:12407202,PMID:15703058,PMID:15908602,PMID:17038516,PMID:17138693,PMID:18650403,PMID:19200151,PMID:20538889,PMID:23264517,locus:2115220;locus_type=protein_coding
