Chr4	Araport11	gene	18071449	18073182	.	-	.	ID=AT4G38680;Name=AT4G38680;Note=glycine rich protein 2;curator_summary=Encodes a glycine-rich protein that binds nucleic acids and promotes DNA melting. Its transcript and protein levels are up-regulated in response to cold treatment with protein levels peaking earlier in shoots (~10-14 days) than in roots (~21 days). It is normally expressed in meristematic regions and developing tissues where cell division occurs. RNAi and antisense lines with lower levels of CSP2/GRP2 transcripts flower earlier than wild type plants and have some defects in anther and seed development.;symbol=GRP2;Alias=ATCSP2,ARABIDOPSIS THALIANA COLD SHOCK PROTEIN 2,CSDP2,COLD SHOCK DOMAIN PROTEIN 2,CSP2,COLD SHOCK PROTEIN 2;full_name=glycine rich protein 2;computational_description=glycine rich protein 2 (GRP2)%3B FUNCTIONS IN: double-stranded DNA binding%2C mRNA binding%2C single-stranded DNA binding%2C nucleic acid binding%3B INVOLVED IN: stamen development%2C vegetative to reproductive phase transition of meristem%2C response to cold%2C seed development%2C DNA duplex unwinding%3B LOCATED IN: nucleolus%2C nucleus%2C plasma membrane%2C cytoplasm%3B EXPRESSED IN: 37 plant structures%3B EXPRESSED DURING: 14 growth stages%3B CONTAINS InterPro DOMAIN/s: Nucleic acid-binding%2C OB-fold-like (InterPro:IPR016027)%2C Nucleic acid-binding%2C OB-fold (InterPro:IPR012340)%2C Cold shock protein (InterPro:IPR011129)%2C Cold-shock conserved site (InterPro:IPR019844)%2C Zinc finger%2C CCHC-type (InterPro:IPR001878)%2C Cold-shock protein%2C DNA-binding (InterPro:IPR002059)%3B BEST Arabidopsis thaliana protein match is: glycine-rich protein 2B (TAIR:AT2G21060.1)%3B Has 150401 Blast hits to 55289 proteins in 3379 species: Archae - 285%3B Bacteria - 51625%3B Metazoa - 48133%3B Fungi - 9113%3B Plants - 13783%3B Viruses - 1771%3B Other Eukaryotes - 25691 (source: NCBI BLink).;Dbxref=PMID:12169696,PMID:12225588,PMID:14595688,PMID:17123099,PMID:17169986,PMID:17828791,PMI